            <ArticleTitle>Cryoanalgesia in the management of chronic facial pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>101-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The results of 85 cryogenic nerve blocks in 43 patients with chronic facial pain over a period of 4 years are reviewed. In 67% of patients with non-herpetic neuralgia the duration of pain relief (median 93 days) exceeded the duration of sensory loss (median 60 days).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
